16 0 obj
<< /A 40 0 R /Alt (Nine-panel figure showing correlations among 12-month changes in body weight, body fat mass, and appendicular skeletal muscle mass in the SGLT2i, GLP-1RA, and GLP-1-on-SGLT2i groups. Panels A\205C show strong positive correlations between changes in body weight and fat mass. Panels D\205F show positive correlations between changes in body weight and muscle mass. Panels G\205I show a significant positive correlation between changes in fat and muscle mass only in the GLP-1RA group, with no significant correlation in the other two groups. Correlation coefficients and p values are displayed, and regression lines indicate statistically significant associations.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 30 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
17 0 obj
<< /A 41 0 R /Alt (Set of nine scatter plots labeled A to I, each showing body recomposition score in kilograms on the y-axis versus HbA1c percentage, eGFR, or age on the x-axis. Panels A, D, and G represent SGLT2i, B, E, and H show GLP-1RA, and C, F, and I show GLP-1-on-SGLT2i treatment groups. Correlation coefficients \(r\) and p-values are displayed on each plot, with A and D marked significant. Linear trend lines are only present in A and D, where a positive correlation is observed.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 31 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
18 0 obj
<< /A 42 0 R /Alt (Three-panel graphic showing ROC curves comparing the predictive performance of SGLT2i \(blue solid\), GLP-1RA \(red dashed\), and GLP-1-on-SGLT2i \(green dash-dot\) for HbA1c \(panel A\), eGFR \(panel B\), and age \(panel C\). Area under the curve \(AUC\) values are highest for SGLT2i in HbA1c \(0.94\), moderate for eGFR \(0.78\), and low for all groups in age \(approximately 0.55\2050.58\). Sensitivity and specificity axes are labeled, with a diagonal reference line present in each plot.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 32 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
